=== P3 Shared surface 0222 PinButton (Android) ===
note: gradlew invoked as gradlew.bat (Windows runner).
note: the Gradle module is :android (settings.gradle.kts maps projectDir=app); the prompt gate's :app:
      placeholder is this repo's :android: module - the same adaptation every sibling P3/A* gate records
      (e.g. 0207 CopyButton, 0183 VehiclePicker).
note: surface ships as flat files under com/teslasync/shared-surfaces/PinButton/ (the prompt's allowed-files
      PinButton.* path is a directory bundle, matching the 0207 CopyButton precedent); the mandated leaf
      cannot form a valid Kotlin package (hyphen segment + PascalCase leaf), so the package is
      io.teslasync.android.sharedsurfaces.pinbutton with @file:Suppress(InvalidPackageDeclaration). Tests
      live in the matching real package path under test/ and androidTest/.
note: capability OK - Kotlin 2.4.0 (>= the prompt's 2.2.x minimum), AGP 8.9.2, Compose BOM 2026.04.01 +
      Material 3, JDK 21 (Android Studio jbr). NOT blocked.
note: P1/S8 wiring - usePinned/useTogglePin map to the shared-core PinnedStore, which is ALREADY wired into
      DataContainer.pinnedStore (registered by the 0183 VehiclePicker slice). The surface consumes it via
      LocalDataContainer.current.pinnedStore; pinned() is the read feed, togglePin() the mutation, refreshAll()
      the retry. No DataContainer edit was needed and no shared file was touched (git status: only the three
      new pinbutton directories).
note: i18n reuses existing P1/S10 catalog keys (translation_pin_{pin,pinned,unpin},
      translation_toast_pin_{pinned,unpinned}_{success,error}, translation_mqtt_stale,
      translation_common_{offline,retry,loading}, translation_freshness_updating) - all present in values/,
      values-ar/ and values-he/. apps/android strings.xml is GENERATED from apps/shared/i18n; editing it would
      drift and is out of allowed-files scope.
note: parity adaptation (covenant #9, logged) - the web `PinOff` lucide glyph has no TeslaGlyphs entry and
      that set is outside this surface's allowed files, so the pinned state is conveyed exactly as the native
      atomic PinButton already does: the single TeslaGlyphs.Pin glyph tinted with the warning/amber status
      token plus the label/tooltip/aria switch. The semantic flip (icon meaning + color + spoken name) is
      reproduced.
note: state matrix - the pin feed is a real cache-then-network read, but the web defaults the list to `[]`
      and ALWAYS renders the button, so the read lifecycle is surfaced ADDITIVELY without hiding the toggle:
      first-load busy indicator, unpinned/pinned content (an empty pin list is the unpinned content state, not
      a blank box), disabled pending toggle, stale/offline/updating freshness chip, and a Retry affordance
      beside the still-usable button on a hard error - the same "render every state, hide no region" contract
      the 0183 VehiclePicker slice honours.
note: androidTest - the :android: androidTest source set has PRE-EXISTING, unrelated compilation breakage
      across many widget/feature/shared-surface UI tests (a Compose-test API drift: assertExists/
      assertDoesNotExist/onAllNodes moved off top-level, plus a NoopLogger reference) that predates this slice
      and is outside its allowed files. The P3 gate does NOT compile androidTest (assembleRelease +
      testReleaseUnitTest + ktlintCheck + detekt only); ktlintCheck DOES lint the androidTest source set and
      passes over PinButtonUiTest.kt. PinButtonUiTest.kt itself is written to the proven 0207 CopyButton UI
      pattern (member-call .assertDoesNotExist(), no broken import).
note: an initial ktlintTestSourceSetCheck run flagged 4 chain-continuation findings in the two unit-test
      files; resolved by extracting the intermediate locals (the same `val state = model.state.value` shape
      the 0183 VehiclePicker test uses). Re-run is green below. No red was committed.

